---
import SolutionPage from '../../components/SolutionPage.astro';
---

<SolutionPage
  title="Broker Research Scored in Public — PSX"
  h1="Broker calls, graded against what happened"
  description="Every public target price and rating from Pakistani research houses, timestamped and scored against the outcome. Measured on the same bar as everyone else."
  path="/solutions/psx-broker-research-scorecard/"
  kicker="For brokers & institutions"
  icon="portfolio"
  lead="Nobody in Pakistan grades sell-side research against what the price actually did. The desk does, publicly, including its own."
  problem="Research houses publish target prices constantly and almost nobody checks them afterwards. A call that was badly wrong two years ago carries the same apparent authority today as one that was right, because the record simply is not kept. That is comfortable for whoever was wrong and expensive for everyone reading."
  appPlan={null}
  ctaLabel="Contact sales"
  features={[
    {
      icon: 'board',
      title: 'Every public call captured',
      body: 'Target prices, ratings and sector views as reported in the business press, turned into structured claims with a date and a testable outcome.',
    },
    {
      icon: 'method',
      title: 'Scored on the outcome, not the narrative',
      body: 'A claim is graded against what the price did by the date it named. No retroactive reinterpretation, no quiet withdrawal.',
    },
    {
      icon: 'research',
      title: 'The desk is on the same board',
      body: 'Henneth’s own calls are scored by the identical method and sit on the same leaderboard. A scorecard that exempts its author is marketing.',
    },
  ]}
  faqs={[
    {
      q: 'Whose calls are being scored?',
      a: 'Pakistani research houses, using their publicly reported calls — the ones already in the business press. Nothing confidential and nothing behind a client paywall is used.',
    },
    {
      q: 'Can a desk have its own calls scored?',
      a: 'Yes. That is what the Broker plan is for: your desk’s calls tracked and graded on the same public leaderboard as everyone else, on the same method.',
    },
    {
      q: 'What if a call was right for the wrong reason?',
      a: 'It still scores as right. The scorecard measures outcomes against dated claims, not reasoning quality — because outcomes are checkable and reasoning quality is an argument.',
    },
    {
      q: 'How is a claim decided to be wrong?',
      a: 'By the price on the date the claim named. Where a call carries no date or no falsifiable target, it is recorded as unscoreable rather than being graded generously.',
    },
  ]}
>
  <h2 class="mid-h">See it before you contact us</h2>
  <p class="mid-p">
    The <a href="/research/">public scorecard</a> is readable without an account. It is the single
    most useful thing to look at before deciding whether this desk is worth talking to — including
    the entries where the desk itself was wrong.
  </p>
  <p class="mid-p">
    For team seats, onboarding and having your desk's calls tracked, the
    <a href="/contact">Broker plan starts with a conversation</a>.
  </p>
</SolutionPage>

<style>
  .mid-h { font-size: 16px; margin: 0 0 12px; }
  .mid-p { font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--ink-2); max-width: 68ch; margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .mid-p a { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
</style>
